on: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318224\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319958\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsNativeDragTarget.cpp"], "git_node": "097aa515d52c8306a92c281f90f83a0c9c797a85", "git_parents": ["28082ff921481f455e9b45c664c25955f6d31baf"], "node": "e87ea0ccad3d1673ab804c82a81e6be2dc4cf836", "parents": ["9eb5e45a6192fedf7898964112007845ab72a3c1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787855697, "git_changesets": ["097aa515d52c8306a92c281f90f83a0c9c797a85"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "423": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063814 - Handle \\ correctly in SplitMimetype  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319097\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320017\n", "files": ["dom/base/MimeType.cpp"], "git_node": "b3d41f5e4c76eceaf966c9a2b2429a30e46f1eb9", "git_parents": ["097aa515d52c8306a92c281f90f83a0c9c797a85"], "node": "c9b010f7d758204ee09e75e107fcd7f48afabcc2", "parents": ["e87ea0ccad3d1673ab804c82a81e6be2dc4cf836"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787855716, "git_changesets": ["b3d41f5e4c76eceaf966c9a2b2429a30e46f1eb9"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "424": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064026 - Check if iterator has reached the end of the string  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319073\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320016\n", "files": ["dom/base/MimeType.cpp"], "git_node": "4bd0a0d0dbbe64f24ef1c45244a53b189f432c0f", "git_parents": ["b3d41f5e4c76eceaf966c9a2b2429a30e46f1eb9"], "node": "7ba6aa04b189cdd0b43415fe313a609e307f4d85", "parents": ["c9b010f7d758204ee09e75e107fcd7f48afabcc2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787855841, "git_changesets": ["4bd0a0d0dbbe64f24ef1c45244a53b189f432c0f"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "425": {"changesets": [{"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061231 - Use PathCchCanonicalize in WinUtils::CanonicalizePath.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nPathCchCanonicalize is documented by Microsoft as preferable to\nPathCanonicalize, for buffer safety reasons.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318223\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320221\n", "files": ["widget/windows/WinUtils.cpp", "widget/windows/WinUtils.h", "widget/windows/moz.build", "widget/windows/tests/gtest/TestWinUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "7abdb9018d0f3f728f02d264c727136660f2473b", "git_parents": ["4bd0a0d0dbbe64f24ef1c45244a53b189f432c0f"], "node": "4f28b669acc9d30daa3eba94bb65d20ea1ac7b76", "parents": ["7ba6aa04b189cdd0b43415fe313a609e307f4d85"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787855875, "git_changesets": ["7abdb9018d0f3f728f02d264c727136660f2473b"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "426": {"changesets": [{"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "[ESR 153] Bug 2050150 - Require an NV12 destination stride that can hold a chroma row.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320550\n", "files": ["dom/media/ImageConversion.cpp", "dom/media/ImageConversion.h"], "git_node": "62068e3c3fae7880cb0115c4fbe3b24714ed8b04", "git_parents": ["7abdb9018d0f3f728f02d264c727136660f2473b"], "node": "0d59c5cd61de15623bbbfedb5dd853c8af85a2a8", "parents": ["4f28b669acc9d30daa3eba94bb65d20ea1ac7b76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "[ESR 153] Bug 2050150 - Decline odd-width configs in the WMF encoder module.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320551\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFDataEncoderUtils.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFDataEncoderUtils.h", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFEncoderModule.cpp"], "git_node": "ce4a0c2359899fdf76cb563dc97038b2275566ac", "git_parents": ["62068e3c3fae7880cb0115c4fbe3b24714ed8b04"], "node": "f3357e9ad7eee57c5193866ce0babbb35b6dd39a", "parents": ["0d59c5cd61de15623bbbfedb5dd853c8af85a2a8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787856361, "git_changesets": ["62068e3c3fae7880cb0115c4fbe3b24714ed8b04", "ce4a0c2359899fdf76cb563dc97038b2275566ac"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "427": {"changesets": [{"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062451 - Add gtest for YUVBufferGenerator's chroma plane sizing.  a=dmeehan\n\nInit() sizes its source buffer from the luma plane length, while the image\ncreators lay out two chroma planes of ceil(width / 2) x ceil(height / 2). Those\ntwo agree only when both dimensions are even.\n\nThe test asserts every chroma byte of the generated image holds the value Init()\nwrote, at odd and even sizes. It fails until the following patch.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317992\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320236\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestYUVBufferGenerator.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "d70c78ae5e7ad949935efa9ed1479ad8243f7ce1", "git_parents": ["ce4a0c2359899fdf76cb563dc97038b2275566ac"], "node": "12428ee864b5f86869c08144604dcc576d6b8f32", "parents": ["f3357e9ad7eee57c5193866ce0babbb35b6dd39a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062451 - Size YUVBufferGenerator's source buffer for odd dimensions.  a=dmeehan\n\nInit() derived the chroma region from the luma plane length, which matches the\nI420 chroma size only when both dimensions are even.\n\nBoth Init() and CreateI420Image now take the chroma size from gfx::ChromaSize(),\nthe helper PlanarYCbCrData::CbCrDataSize() already uses, so the buffer size and\nthe plane layout cannot disagree. That removes the four hand-rolled (x + 1) / 2\nexpressions this file carried, which is what let the two sides drift apart.\n\nPre-existing rather than a regression: the expression has been here at least\nsince it moved into this file in bug 1423253, and every current caller passes\neven dimensions, for which the old and new forms are numerically identical.\nVideoFrameConverterTest, MediaDataEncoder and VideoTrackEncoder pass unchanged.\n\nMakes the preceding test pass.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317993\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320237\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/YUVBufferGenerator.cpp"], "git_node": "93799770744cfb77bfa8d3b7cb019d1af1e5b7c0", "git_parents": ["d70c78ae5e7ad949935efa9ed1479ad8243f7ce1"], "node": "66901cf855e4ff5423e2b8d3106c77c176117089", "parents": ["12428ee864b5f86869c08144604dcc576d6b8f32"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787856837, "git_changesets": ["d70c78ae5e7ad949935efa9ed1479ad8243f7ce1", "93799770744cfb77bfa8d3b7cb019d1af1e5b7c0"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "428": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045293 - [devtools] Disable about:debugging tests starting ADB on macos 1500  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320029\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321500\n", "files": ["devtools/client/aboutdebugging/test/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "ac3a7dc5b6b32303366762675e0891576af3ab9c", "git_parents": ["93799770744cfb77bfa8d3b7cb019d1af1e5b7c0"], "node": "56e3963c89364fb8e88c2dca2d977c9f5bdac257", "parents": ["66901cf855e4ff5423e2b8d3106c77c176117089"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787864462, "git_changesets": ["ac3a7dc5b6b32303366762675e0891576af3ab9c"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "429": {"changesets": [{"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050017 - Point the aiwindow browser tests at a local search engine  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320303\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321669\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "dc8d0becbc3cea3ad17676888d482962139403b6", "git_parents": ["ac3a7dc5b6b32303366762675e0891576af3ab9c"], "node": "126f8fdae66b02284662f690d90834eede6b5e29", "parents": ["56e3963c89364fb8e88c2dca2d977c9f5bdac257"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787864500, "git_changesets": ["dc8d0becbc3cea3ad17676888d482962139403b6"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "430": {"changesets": [{"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064601 - Improve processing of feConvolveMatrix kernelMatrix  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320032\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321795\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/FilterNodeSoftware.cpp"], "git_node": "de9bf5874b2707295d688e65ae6a80732ad86701", "git_parents": ["dc8d0becbc3cea3ad17676888d482962139403b6"], "node": "a32b10259529519d741b95a4ec0ff406b1430423", "parents": ["126f8fdae66b02284662f690d90834eede6b5e29"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787864629, "git_changesets": ["de9bf5874b2707295d688e65ae6a80732ad86701"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "431": {"changesets": [{"author": "Maurice Dauer \u003cmdauer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063539 - Always resolve special target names,  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318844\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319952\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp"], "git_node": "4b71aa84a43d735584c2701f9ae78a3b636bf6cd", "git_parents": ["de9bf5874b2707295d688e65ae6a80732ad86701"], "node": "9c5c01839a828a5da0e96d54e102fd085087a912", "parents": ["a32b10259529519d741b95a4ec0ff406b1430423"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787864648, "git_changesets": ["4b71aa84a43d735584c2701f9ae78a3b636bf6cd"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "432": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andreas Farre \u003cfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054670 - Check target for session store updates.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319099\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320088\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/sessionstore/SessionStoreParent.cpp", "toolkit/components/sessionstore/SessionStoreParent.h"], "git_node": "361aa5d42da8afad32448fbe55d978d450a60abf", "git_parents": ["4b71aa84a43d735584c2701f9ae78a3b636bf6cd"], "node": "3bf91ad508947f6bb0c9bf3932a2cbc1b47771ec", "parents": ["9c5c01839a828a5da0e96d54e102fd085087a912"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787864668, "git_changesets": ["361aa5d42da8afad32448fbe55d978d450a60abf"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "433": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062527 - Respect the disable-extension policy in the add-ons sync engine.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nThe install path needs a check of its own: at onInstallStarted the add-on is\nnot in the database yet, so the AddonManager enforcement later in this stack\ndoes not cover it.\n\nIncoming records are skipped rather than failed, so this client keeps\ndisagreeing with the server record and will later upload enabled: true,\nre-enabling the add-on on clients that are not under policy. That is preferred\nto failing the record and retrying it on every sync.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318136\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320261\n", "files": ["services/sync/modules/addonutils.sys.mjs", "services/sync/modules/engines/addons.sys.mjs", "services/sync/tests/unit/test_addon_utils.js", "services/sync/tests/unit/test_addons_store.js"], "git_node": "5dc61902a355714f7490f4eae9d5bafbfd8f470b", "git_parents": ["361aa5d42da8afad32448fbe55d978d450a60abf"], "node": "e834385de1103d9696e79e19828c9f02770f6e65", "parents": ["3bf91ad508947f6bb0c9bf3932a2cbc1b47771ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062527 - Hide the disable-extension button for policy-locked extensions.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318137\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320262\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/extensionControlled.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/chrome/test_setting_control_extension_controlled.html", "browser/components/preferences/widgets/setting-control/setting-control.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/widgets/setting-control/setting-control.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/preferences/Setting.mjs"], "git_node": "05dff920a87ecad0918ae0d8b2c35961caf2e560", "git_parents": ["5dc61902a355714f7490f4eae9d5bafbfd8f470b"], "node": "2091debe09e3d7a36b480580326a627bf96d2f27", "parents": ["e834385de1103d9696e79e19828c9f02770f6e65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062527 - Enforce the disable-extension policy in the Add-ons Manager.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nmanagement.setEnabled tests the policy directly instead of PERM_CAN_DISABLE.\nThat permission bit is also missing for appDisabled add-ons, already-disabled\nadd-ons and the default theme, so relying on it would throw for calls that used\nto do nothing.\n\nThe tab-hide doorhanger is not shown at all for a locked add-on, since disabling\nis the only action it offers. This matches the existing handling of\ndistribution-installed add-ons.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318138\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320263\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_extensions.js", "browser/components/extensions/ExtensionControlledPopup.sys.mjs", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_tabs_hide.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-management.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_management_policy.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIDatabase.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "4053b4bd0afdece3c7be4d5c5af81bb026333e7e", "git_parents": ["05dff920a87ecad0918ae0d8b2c35961caf2e560"], "node": "fec2670d0f7513d584b99725cf8acddd2ddb62d7", "parents": ["2091debe09e3d7a36b480580326a627bf96d2f27"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787864724, "git_changesets": ["5dc61902a355714f7490f4eae9d5bafbfd8f470b", "05dff920a87ecad0918ae0d8b2c35961caf2e560", "4053b4bd0afdece3c7be4d5c5af81bb026333e7e"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "434": {"changesets": [{"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062812 - Drop virtual from nsIWidget::(Start|Stop)AsyncAutoscroll.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nStartAsyncAutoscroll and StopAsyncAutoscroll don't have to be virtual.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320260\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320468\n", "files": ["widget/nsIWidget.h"], "git_node": "eb61d203a0a8e07aa008ed623e6206c9a80214bd", "git_parents": ["4053b4bd0afdece3c7be4d5c5af81bb026333e7e"], "node": "b0541a803ae0afe367eef466a5a97c8963db8f6a", "parents": ["fec2670d0f7513d584b99725cf8acddd2ddb62d7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787864745, "git_changesets": ["eb61d203a0a8e07aa008ed623e6206c9a80214bd"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "435": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dominik Bay \u003cdominik@bay.sh\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066736 - Validate filter array lengths in FilePickerParent::RecvOpen.  a=dmeehan\n\nThe loop in RecvOpen counts with aFilters.Length() but reads\naFilterNames[i]. If a content process sends the message with more filters\nthan filterNames, the read goes out of bounds and the parent process\ncrashes. So I added a check that both arrays have the same length.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321511\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321697\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/FilePickerParent.cpp"], "git_node": "41400e2532fcb8e441d2300e3803bcbf575f0421", "git_parents": ["eb61d203a0a8e07aa008ed623e6206c9a80214bd"], "node": "a5e94f957178d7ebd27ee22e5e77efa1951ef4fe", "parents": ["b0541a803ae0afe367eef466a5a97c8963db8f6a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787865135, "git_changesets": ["41400e2532fcb8e441d2300e3803bcbf575f0421"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "436": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058417 - Use the normalized format consistently in DataTransfer::SetDataAtInternal.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320206\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320894\n", "files": ["dom/events/DataTransfer.cpp"], "git_node": "c53fe556731b1bbbf29c780a2d72a1486116d2f0", "git_parents": ["41400e2532fcb8e441d2300e3803bcbf575f0421"], "node": "cab50a6fda9bade24c691a3cb0b99ef67cea5f8e", "parents": ["a5e94f957178d7ebd27ee22e5e77efa1951ef4fe"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787870110, "git_changesets": ["c53fe556731b1bbbf29c780a2d72a1486116d2f0"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "437": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066329.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321445\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321773\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/swgl/src/swgl_ext.h"], "git_node": "d81d3113f0f19739787e3cbc754b2d20d4edfd36", "git_parents": ["c53fe556731b1bbbf29c780a2d72a1486116d2f0"], "node": "59535579dd6d2e0240a3b61054c14a4932b85458", "parents": ["cab50a6fda9bade24c691a3cb0b99ef67cea5f8e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787870129, "git_changesets": ["d81d3113f0f19739787e3cbc754b2d20d4edfd36"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "438": {"changesets": [{"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058790 - adjust desktop reader mode URL handling,  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321557\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321747\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/reader/ReaderMode.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b198bedd2780e8e6f926d28b0e95978a4137343d", "git_parents": ["d81d3113f0f19739787e3cbc754b2d20d4edfd36"], "node": "a2b65e978c4b2563a04fd7e9dd6df1ba16bbca8b", "parents": ["59535579dd6d2e0240a3b61054c14a4932b85458"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787870150, "git_changesets": ["b198bedd2780e8e6f926d28b0e95978a4137343d"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "439": {"changesets": [{"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057990: Part 1 - Check Windows DROPFILES data  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nAdds nsClipboard::IsValidDropFilesData to sanity check that we were given a\nvalid DROPFILES structure.  An invalid structure would have to be posted\nby whatever application owns the clipboard or starts the drag; Gecko's own\nwriter always emits a well-formed DROPFILES.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321431\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsClipboard.cpp", "widget/windows/nsClipboard.h", "widget/windows/nsDragService.cpp", "widget/windows/tests/gtest/TestWinDND.cpp"], "git_node": "8a5165ae3dc126a705e071e525ca540efcc05721", "git_parents": ["b198bedd2780e8e6f926d28b0e95978a4137343d"], "node": "d7c89804cc7fcb87cf67b6b52e676591a9d13131", "parents": ["a2b65e978c4b2563a04fd7e9dd6df1ba16bbca8b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787870186, "git_changesets": ["8a5165ae3dc126a705e071e525ca540efcc05721"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "440": {"changesets": [{"author": "Maurice Dauer \u003cmdauer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058065 - Truncate on on unexpected error,  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321513\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321629\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLTextureUpload.cpp"], "git_node": "342dd4fe9d09eb1e17ab393ae8d0382d72661d0f", "git_parents": ["8a5165ae3dc126a705e071e525ca540efcc05721"], "node": "95b3be70040626cf3c11c7daefff08a59aac26bc", "parents": ["d7c89804cc7fcb87cf67b6b52e676591a9d13131"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787870264, "git_changesets": ["342dd4fe9d09eb1e17ab393ae8d0382d72661d0f"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "441": {"changesets": [{"author": "Maurice Dauer \u003cmdauer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058064 - Validate vertexAttribPointer byteOffset,  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321487\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321596\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContextVertices.cpp"], "git_node": "2c9c69d3bbe4700343bef59ddcbe986b92a66a79", "git_parents": ["342dd4fe9d09eb1e17ab393ae8d0382d72661d0f"], "node": "78e4d8792d5ee2c099519ffaf92e705bceef30fa", "parents": ["95b3be70040626cf3c11c7daefff08a59aac26bc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787870284, "git_changesets": ["2c9c69d3bbe4700343bef59ddcbe986b92a66a79"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "442": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061257 - Return early if the chunk length is unexpected in ProtocoalParserV2.  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320442\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321485\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/url-classifier/ProtocolParser.cpp"], "git_node": "50fd2c5e44646b44986fbdf3934160bd0adac3cf", "git_parents": ["2c9c69d3bbe4700343bef59ddcbe986b92a66a79"], "node": "45a96de2ae52d6ca7d1a5ea44b8098c8f73e92dc", "parents": ["78e4d8792d5ee2c099519ffaf92e705bceef30fa"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787873741, "git_changesets": ["50fd2c5e44646b44986fbdf3934160bd0adac3cf"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "443": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andy Leiserson \u003caleiserson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059599 - WebGPU tests not running on MacOS in release branch CI  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319268\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320522\n", "files": ["dom/webgpu/tests/mochitest/mochitest-disabled.toml", "dom/webgpu/tests/mochitest/mochitest-no-pref.toml", "dom/webgpu/tests/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "e0813adb975eb69c5f609e4fdd12877454886f92", "git_parents": ["50fd2c5e44646b44986fbdf3934160bd0adac3cf"], "node": "9db6851c11bfc89f06b605087e0c3fdca36134a9", "parents": ["45a96de2ae52d6ca7d1a5ea44b8098c8f73e92dc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787875196, "git_changesets": ["e0813adb975eb69c5f609e4fdd12877454886f92"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "444": {"changesets": [{"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042302 - Make AutoHandlingUserInputStatePusher main-thread-only;  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nThe user input state is only available on main thread, so AutoHandlingUserInputStatePusher\ncan also be main-thread-only.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313184\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320488\n", "files": ["dom/base/UserActivation.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSContext.cpp"], "git_node": "52901a11351f1b2af67c936e2b1909d8e27a3047", "git_parents": ["e0813adb975eb69c5f609e4fdd12877454886f92"], "node": "0bfae0431e0f0680a57c4513f3b38e71117cea4d", "parents": ["9db6851c11bfc89f06b605087e0c3fdca36134a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042302 - Skip the paste confirmation popup if programmatic paste is initiated while handling a keyboard event that would trigger a paste command;  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nWhen a page requests to read the clipboard programmatically and the clipboard\ndata originates from a different page, a paste popup is shown to obtain user\nconsent. However, if the programmatic paste is initiated while handling a\nkeyboard event that would trigger a paste command, it is not necessary to ask\nfor confirmation, since we know the page could already obtain the clipboard data\nfrom paste event.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308747\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320489\n", "files": ["dom/base/UserActivation.cpp", "dom/base/UserActivation.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowCommands.cpp", "dom/events/GlobalKeyListener.cpp", "dom/events/GlobalKeyListener.h", "dom/events/KeyEventHandler.cpp", "dom/events/KeyEventHandler.h", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser.toml", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser_document_command_paste_contextmenu_event_loop.js", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser_document_command_paste_contextmenu_suppression_key.js", "dom/events/test/gtest/TestShortcutKeyDefinitions.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorCommands.cpp", "widget/TextEventDispatcher.cpp", "widget/TextEvents.h", "widget/nsGUIEventIPC.h"], "git_node": "4a861a0e9b304ee8ed9f37429972755d1233f654", "git_parents": ["52901a11351f1b2af67c936e2b1909d8e27a3047"], "node": "0cabea446d16607bb139971cf933cecb05587c2f", "parents": ["0bfae0431e0f0680a57c4513f3b38e71117cea4d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787875222, "git_changesets": ["52901a11351f1b2af67c936e2b1909d8e27a3047", "4a861a0e9b304ee8ed9f37429972755d1233f654"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "445": {"changesets": [{"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057352 - Use a dedicated logic for each nested resource update.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313895\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320851\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/commands/resource/moz.build", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/nested-update-processors/moz.build", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/nested-update-processors/stylesheet.js", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/resource-command.js"], "git_node": "9c24d75f15fcaddf2f1cedd1cd0175b66bd3eb06", "git_parents": ["4a861a0e9b304ee8ed9f37429972755d1233f654"], "node": "a524ada058938b32f6b3dd86afa8c4a91ec8a62b", "parents": ["0cabea446d16607bb139971cf933cecb05587c2f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787875259, "git_changesets": ["9c24d75f15fcaddf2f1cedd1cd0175b66bd3eb06"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "446": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059196 - Set the ongoing navigation to the navigation ID also for javascript: URLs.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320058\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320890\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/precommit-handler/precommitHandler-javascript-url-before-commit.html"], "git_node": "ed7ce333f055d9619727a3645a2a81ca1cb5f147", "git_parents": ["9c24d75f15fcaddf2f1cedd1cd0175b66bd3eb06"], "node": "cd9d5276b3f5b43586f0f9a9b97e5a71393a0bd5", "parents": ["a524ada058938b32f6b3dd86afa8c4a91ec8a62b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787875287, "git_changesets": ["ed7ce333f055d9619727a3645a2a81ca1cb5f147"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "447": {"changesets": [{"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063652 - [devtools] Escape HTML entities when rendering Local Mode listings.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319949\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321172\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkLocalMode.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "adbd1d7a89a41c5aad2872a697a839f658dcb2cb", "git_parents": ["ed7ce333f055d9619727a3645a2a81ca1cb5f147"], "node": "7ce99e1da71755263a42e4f899cc16631451cc31", "parents": ["cd9d5276b3f5b43586f0f9a9b97e5a71393a0bd5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787875315, "git_changesets": ["adbd1d7a89a41c5aad2872a697a839f658dcb2cb"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "448": {"changesets": [{"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062551 - Allow heapsnapshot records when DevTools are active.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318392\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321173\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/heapsnapshot/HeapSnapshotTempFileHelperParent.cpp", "devtools/shared/heapsnapshot/tests/xpcshell/test_saveHeapSnapshot_e10s_01.js"], "git_node": "3a6999e5c06733b1f38e54001f4787a90fbbee7e", "git_parents": ["adbd1d7a89a41c5aad2872a697a839f658dcb2cb"], "node": "95855c3fcaea3f7ca4b3231cd27a56b2ffd2d6a1", "parents": ["7ce99e1da71755263a42e4f899cc16631451cc31"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787875393, "git_changesets": ["3a6999e5c06733b1f38e54001f4787a90fbbee7e"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "449": {"changesets": [{"author": "Maurice Dauer \u003cmdauer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065397 - Add bounds check hardening to _cairo_array_index,  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320349\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321530\n", "files": ["gfx/cairo/cairo/src/cairo-array.c", "gfx/cairo/patches/0050-Bug-2065397-array-bounds-check.patch"], "git_node": "23e276143af753209c732522d0eeac0e12deb8aa", "git_parents": ["3a6999e5c06733b1f38e54001f4787a90fbbee7e"], "node": "81019399e280541ab3dcfb80d8d342d59c4f9b0c", "parents": ["95855c3fcaea3f7ca4b3231cd27a56b2ffd2d6a1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787878999, "git_changesets": ["23e276143af753209c732522d0eeac0e12deb8aa"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "450": {"changesets": [{"author": "Pier Angelo Vendrame \u003cpierov@torproject.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063031 - Spoof video PiP size under RFP.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318184\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320862\n", "files": ["dom/media/PictureInPictureWindow.cpp", "dom/media/PictureInPictureWindow.h", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLVideoElement.cpp", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLVideoElement.h", "toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/tests/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/tests/browser_resistFingerprinting.js"], "git_node": "20df84b487350bb29434094bc27f1d7d70a5f949", "git_parents": ["23e276143af753209c732522d0eeac0e12deb8aa"], "node": "b69995b602a0312b0d4bdb0c4ce2810e4cef7da1", "parents": ["81019399e280541ab3dcfb80d8d342d59c4f9b0c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787920350, "git_changesets": ["20df84b487350bb29434094bc27f1d7d70a5f949"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "451": {"changesets": [{"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052664 - Consider a history entry which is being replaced by a dropped link on it's tab as having user iteraction.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312105\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320943\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/drag-and-drop.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser.toml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_drop_link_user_interaction.js"], "git_node": "138cdd5c36e9aae4bf37c6ad3eed1870d0005dcd", "git_parents": ["20df84b487350bb29434094bc27f1d7d70a5f949"], "node": "effe4de3dd9f3ddc730cb89a0c890c1e3b77ca4d", "parents": ["b69995b602a0312b0d4bdb0c4ce2810e4cef7da1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787920373, "git_changesets": ["138cdd5c36e9aae4bf37c6ad3eed1870d0005dcd"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "452": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066155 - Cap the cookie database WAL at 512KB instead of 2MB  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321089\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321721\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/cookie/CookiePersistentStorage.cpp"], "git_node": "242a4460114e2450a13820601f71e8f296823891", "git_parents": ["138cdd5c36e9aae4bf37c6ad3eed1870d0005dcd"], "node": "8edb16c827316231a2ef1d04d0e8843a3782581f", "parents": ["effe4de3dd9f3ddc730cb89a0c890c1e3b77ca4d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787920416, "git_changesets": ["242a4460114e2450a13820601f71e8f296823891"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "453": {"changesets": [{"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061788 - Make `HTMLEditor::InsertFromDataTransfer` use the almost same order as `HTMLTransferablePreparer::AddDataFlavorsInBestOrder`  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nWhen we create a `DataTransfer` from `nsITransferable`,\n`HTMLTransferablePreparer::AddDataFlavorsInBestOrder` adds the data\nwith preferred order of `HTMLEditor`. However,\n`HTMLEditor::InsertFromDataTransfer` is called with `DataTransfer`\ncreated outside `HTMLEditor`. Therefore, the order can be any.\nHowever, `HTMLEditor` should use the same order as far as possible.\n\nHowever, the coming `DataTransfer`'s data order may be meaningful\nespecially when it's an image because converting image format may be\nlossy conversion. Therefore, this patch does not reorder the images\nwith `clipboard.paste_image_type` pref to keep current behavior.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318030\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321775\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDataTransfer.cpp", "editor/libeditor/tests/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_dragdrop_img_with_data_url.html"], "git_node": "7c07ddea7b064a49a84ca251417d4700c92c0f09", "git_parents": ["242a4460114e2450a13820601f71e8f296823891"], "node": "7e0d8fd51c6a7eef8d0d68a20749b8403d57a67b", "parents": ["8edb16c827316231a2ef1d04d0e8843a3782581f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787920476, "git_changesets": ["7c07ddea7b064a49a84ca251417d4700c92c0f09"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "454": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063089 - part 1: rerun alias analysis after loop unrolling.  .  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nMIR-level loop unrolling can have the effect of making some\nMDefinition::loadDependency_ fields become incorrect.  Fixing them up\nincrementally is not easy, so this patch supplies an alternative fix, which is\nto simply recompute them all, after unrolling is complete, by rerunning alias\nanalysis.\n\nChanges:\n\n* UnrollLoops.cpp: free method UnrollAndOrPeelLoop:\n\n  - remove code to fix up loadDependency_ fields during node cloning.  That\n    code is now known to be insufficient, and leaving it in is misleading.\n\n* UnrollLoops.cpp: free method UnrollLoops:\n\n  - control flow change: make an early exit if we have no final candidate loops\n    to unroll.  This allows a few simplifications of the code that follows.\n\n  - for debug builds, invalidate all the loadDependency_ fields so as to catch\n    any subsequent uses\n\n  - rerun alias analysis after loop unrolling, if unrolling changed anything,\n    by calling AccountForCFGChanges.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319428\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321779\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/UnrollLoops.cpp"], "git_node": "e361ecb4e9af08ddba562d696c5bf31a3b9ac7d2", "git_parents": ["7c07ddea7b064a49a84ca251417d4700c92c0f09"], "node": "625a2b0103b52e225fd1261667af736f8110414b", "parents": ["7e0d8fd51c6a7eef8d0d68a20749b8403d57a67b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787920883, "git_changesets": ["e361ecb4e9af08ddba562d696c5bf31a3b9ac7d2"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "455": {"changesets": [{"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054440 - Make `IMEContentObserver::OnSelectionChange()` treat selection changes during `TextEditor` recreation as caused by composition  a=dmeehan\n\nIf a `TextEditor` is recreated after a reframe and it has composition,\nthe composition including selection will be restored in the new\n`TextEditor` instance as the same as the previous selection. Therefore,\nrestoring `Selection` should be treated as selection changes caused by\nhandling composition.\n\nIf selection is intentionally modified during a reframe, this change\ncould cause a regression. However, when the selection is changed, we\nmay ignore that with preserving the composition. However, it's hard\nto avoid the situation and such web app is anyway not useful for IME\nusers. Therefore, we could try to take this fix until we would fix\nbug 2017201.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312030\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320771\n", "files": ["dom/events/IMEContentObserver.cpp", "dom/events/IMEContentObserver.h", "dom/events/TextComposition.cpp", "dom/html/TextControlState.cpp", "dom/html/TextControlState.h", "editor/libeditor/tests/chrome.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_reframe_text_control_at_compositionstart.html"], "git_node": "dd039a06e35ed298ef34ed71d75b5eabed2e6772", "git_parents": ["e361ecb4e9af08ddba562d696c5bf31a3b9ac7d2"], "node": "6a446d68c2af8d22d0ae89e3f0eccffd05db5089", "parents": ["625a2b0103b52e225fd1261667af736f8110414b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787921143, "git_changesets": ["dd039a06e35ed298ef34ed71d75b5eabed2e6772"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "456": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065080 - Let AsyncShutdown's crash countdown run on wall clock and give it a wider margin over nsTerminator.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nnsTerminator is meant to be the backstop behind AsyncShutdown, but in practice\nit wins the race for the great majority of shutdown hangs, and we then lose the\nAsyncShutdownTimeout annotation that names the blockers we were waiting for.\n\nThe countdown leading to the AsyncShutdown crash resolved after a fixed number\nof delivered timer beats. Its timer is TYPE_REPEATING_PRECISE_CAN_SKIP, which\ndrops undelivered ticks instead of queuing them, so main thread jank, which is\na given during a shutdown hang, stretched the countdown well past the intended\n60 seconds of wall clock. Poll a monotonic deadline instead. A suspended\ncomputer does not advance that clock, so we keep tolerating suspend, but a busy\nmain thread no longer buys extra time. This cannot make us crash where we did\nnot before: the terminator already enforces the same deadline from its own\nthread.\n\nAsyncShutdown also arms its countdown later than the terminator arms its own.\nThe terminator's clock for a phase starts in AdvanceShutdownPhaseInternal,\nbefore KillClearOnShutdown and before any observer of the phase runs, and the\nAsyncShutdown spinner is one of those observers. Widen the terminator's\nadditional wait from 3 to 10 seconds, so that gap, the resolution of the\ncountdown and the time it takes to annotate the crash report all fit into the\nmargin.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320113\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322050\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/asyncshutdown/AsyncShutdown.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/terminator/nsTerminator.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/test/unit/test_crash_AsyncShutdown.js"], "git_node": "f56a76f4f9e1b90a3c87615d6a1ca03600fe230c", "git_parents": ["dd039a06e35ed298ef34ed71d75b5eabed2e6772"], "node": "5463e9d70ead068cb9774e50b6a1b2c14b47451b", "parents": ["6a446d68c2af8d22d0ae89e3f0eccffd05db5089"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787922935, "git_changesets": ["f56a76f4f9e1b90a3c87615d6a1ca03600fe230c"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "457": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063975 - Hide the File menu New Private Window item when private browsing is disabled.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319210\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320213\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/base/content/nonbrowser-mac.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_disable_privatebrowsing.js"], "git_node": "50bb4e5640c56e2433c50d253bc1b242c3a01d4c", "git_parents": ["f56a76f4f9e1b90a3c87615d6a1ca03600fe230c"], "node": "a02b362d8bdc6449fb88c3ea384936643d8a926e", "parents": ["5463e9d70ead068cb9774e50b6a1b2c14b47451b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787922956, "git_changesets": ["50bb4e5640c56e2433c50d253bc1b242c3a01d4c"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "458": {"changesets": [{"author": "Janika \u003cjneuberger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061452 - Disable cookie permission controls in Page Info when set by policy  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nWhen initializing the Cookies row on the Page Info, disable the checkbox and\ncmd_cookieToggle command when scope == SitePermissions.SCOPE_POLICY, in addition to\nthe existing prefIsLocked(\"network.cookie.cookieBehavior\") check. This locks cookie\npermissions set by the Cookies policy (EXPIRE_POLICY), matching the other permissions\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316902\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319823\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/pageinfo/permissions.js", "browser/base/content/test/pageinfo/browser_pageinfo_permissions.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_pageinfo_permissions.js"], "git_node": "10baf79d1176d6a5ba03077e1d87271d0a06a2d8", "git_parents": ["50bb4e5640c56e2433c50d253bc1b242c3a01d4c"], "node": "cfac9a806a9f24a3230c871b73b646134968a1c6", "parents": ["a02b362d8bdc6449fb88c3ea384936643d8a926e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787922976, "git_changesets": ["10baf79d1176d6a5ba03077e1d87271d0a06a2d8"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "459": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1980406 - Add FirefoxHome.Widgets policy for new tab widgets  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316903\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319593\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_firefoxhome.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_simple_pref_policies.js"], "git_node": "d03da844fad816da16d1daea54c8bdedc6784789", "git_parents": ["10baf79d1176d6a5ba03077e1d87271d0a06a2d8"], "node": "a40327c6e5ec90b137e2d78561aeeb4d84d5b956", "parents": ["cfac9a806a9f24a3230c871b73b646134968a1c6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787922996, "git_changesets": ["d03da844fad816da16d1daea54c8bdedc6784789"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "460": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045223 - Hold a local reference to the DistributionCustomizer while applying customizations.  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317543\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319126\n", "files": ["browser/components/distribution.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_distribution_bookmarks_first.js", "browser/components/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "68654e0c518ee42588350ca0ed78e1a2be8d3d6a", "git_parents": ["d03da844fad816da16d1daea54c8bdedc6784789"], "node": "5f391dee366faff09c2f92fab0961a9520079c02", "parents": ["a40327c6e5ec90b137e2d78561aeeb4d84d5b956"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787923222, "git_changesets": ["68654e0c518ee42588350ca0ed78e1a2be8d3d6a"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "461": {"changesets": [{"author": "DonalMe \u003c76789979+DonalMe@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063031 - Fix ESR153 test due to Bug 2052740 a=bustage\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/tests/browser_resistFingerprinting.js"], "git_node": "faeed61e1f1f21bd2863578d50a0cbaa2498a9be", "git_parents": ["68654e0c518ee42588350ca0ed78e1a2be8d3d6a"], "node": "6dad25c1702744d1a5cb951bcb2a1b75b1457169", "parents": ["5f391dee366faff09c2f92fab0961a9520079c02"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787927803, "git_changesets": ["faeed61e1f1f21bd2863578d50a0cbaa2498a9be"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "462": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1830323 - Start a new WebM cluster on an interval, not just on keyframes.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nA SimpleBlock's timecode is relative to the start of its cluster and is\nserialized as an int16_t of milliseconds, so a cluster cannot span more than\n32767ms. EbmlComposer only started a new cluster on a video keyframe when the\nstream had video, so a video track that stalled for longer than that -- while\naudio kept flowing -- made the timecode overflow and crashed.\n\nApply the interval that audio-only streams already used to every stream, since\na video track cannot be relied on to keep producing keyframes. Keyframes still\nstart a cluster, so they remain aligned with one; clusters just no longer wait\nfor one. The WebM muxer guidelines allow this, saying only that keyframes\nSHOULD be placed at the beginning of clusters.\n\nThe block timecode is now bounded by the interval, which a static_assert ties\nto the format limit, so the release assertion on it is replaced by a debug-only\none covering the remaining caller contract: frames in non-decreasing time order.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320118\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321457\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestWebMWriter.cpp", "dom/media/webm/EbmlComposer.cpp"], "git_node": "3eb2a4118a05466373561b76e0d6af78836220e2", "git_parents": ["faeed61e1f1f21bd2863578d50a0cbaa2498a9be"], "node": "6a4633766f43f284bb8c378942c52b03ddfc6440", "parents": ["6dad25c1702744d1a5cb951bcb2a1b75b1457169"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788012328, "git_changesets": ["3eb2a4118a05466373561b76e0d6af78836220e2"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "463": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr153 repo-update HSTS HPKP -  a=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322078\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": "69b805d2f85c3328770b3b1806e2b02b9f926569", "git_parents": ["3eb2a4118a05466373561b76e0d6af78836220e2"], "node": "135fe7bf57e27fda069f183d7c232381b280f7ae", "parents": ["6a4633766f43f284bb8c378942c52b03ddfc6440"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788012555, "git_changesets": ["69b805d2f85c3328770b3b1806e2b02b9f926569"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "464": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058618 - Remove some obsolete stuff from gfxFontEntry.  a=dmeehan\n\n(Preliminary cleanup, no functional change.)\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318732\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322062\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/CoreTextFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFT2FontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxHarfBuzzShaper.cpp"], "git_node": "9b14b0b5bd9a9508e90c2923e361b0e44f9b941d", "git_parents": ["69b805d2f85c3328770b3b1806e2b02b9f926569"], "node": "30b175f380ae569ca37452febce903abb042d444", "parents": ["135fe7bf57e27fda069f183d7c232381b280f7ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058618 - Guard mCharacterMap with the gfxFontEntry's RWLock.  a=dmeehan\n\nIt's kept as an atomic ptr so that we can check for existence without needing to lock;\nwe only need to lock around mutations (write) or dereferencing (read).\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318733\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322063\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/CoreTextFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFT2FontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxHarfBuzzShaper.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxHarfBuzzShaper.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.h"], "git_node": "087e0436a27d3892e04df1f7c687deab45c7a875", "git_parents": ["9b14b0b5bd9a9508e90c2923e361b0e44f9b941d"], "node": "e05dd7eb2e70a7ce3fdfd60c4dd5c1066a57130d", "parents": ["30b175f380ae569ca37452febce903abb042d444"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788012866, "git_changesets": ["9b14b0b5bd9a9508e90c2923e361b0e44f9b941d", "087e0436a27d3892e04df1f7c687deab45c7a875"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "465": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andreas Farre \u003cfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029482 - Don't make ORB exemptions for DevTools.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319804\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322302\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp"], "git_node