g 2027336 - Always call forget.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322230\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322283\n", "files": ["intl/components/src/RelativeTimeFormat.cpp"], "git_node": "2d425e091aff57a1ee1ba9876c3533ffd8e2afaf", "git_parents": ["cb654f5bbca210c19273b6239c8379d22746b471"], "node": "441c2002bd9901576d11c7525ab84f567498c0f3", "parents": ["d22dd4a081b58433e339de3f97bf35fa1a013e58"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788194384, "git_changesets": ["2d425e091aff57a1ee1ba9876c3533ffd8e2afaf"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "469": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr153 repo-update remote-settings tld-suffixes ct-logs -  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322232\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/ai-window-prompts.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/translations-models.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": "77f9a372b3d11d98c109ed149354525ec4d89c36", "git_parents": ["2d425e091aff57a1ee1ba9876c3533ffd8e2afaf"], "node": "45170689fe65e3a76c4332577e2f00a9117189ae", "parents": ["441c2002bd9901576d11c7525ab84f567498c0f3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788194405, "git_changesets": ["77f9a372b3d11d98c109ed149354525ec4d89c36"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "470": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064328 - Update h2  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319479\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322248\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/h2/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/h2/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/h2/.github/workflows/CI.yml", "third_party/rust/h2/CHANGELOG.md", "third_party/rust/h2/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/h2/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/h2/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/h2/benches/main.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/client.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/codec/framed_read.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/codec/framed_write.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/codec/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/frame/data.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/frame/headers.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/frame/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/fuzz_bridge.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/decoder.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/encoder.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/huffman/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/huffman/table.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/test/fixture.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/test/fuzz.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/connection.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/counts.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/prioritize.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/recv.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/send.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/state.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/stream.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/streams.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/server.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/share.rs"], "git_node": "b221ec65c96a0a333db533571ad749a68796faef", "git_parents": ["77f9a372b3d11d98c109ed149354525ec4d89c36"], "node": "302fbfe9a9dfcb5f2f77c58f0ffb0cb9880b233f", "parents": ["45170689fe65e3a76c4332577e2f00a9117189ae"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788195068, "git_changesets": ["b221ec65c96a0a333db533571ad749a68796faef"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "471": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064321 - Emit repetitions for the surface's needs, not the tile cache dirty rect.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nprepare_repeatable_quad's \"repeat by duplicating the primitive\" path enumerated\nrepetitions against frame_state.current_dirty_region(), which is the picture\ncache tile's dirty region: push_dirty_region only happens for\nPictureCompositeMode::TileCache. Inside an intermediate surface that samples\noutside of its own footprint, the repetitions falling in that surface's\ninflation margin were dropped, so a blur read missing content and the wrong\nresult was baked into the picture cache tile with nothing left to invalidate it.\n\nCull against the current surface's clipping_rect instead. For a primitive drawn\nstraight onto a picture cache slice that is the dirty region (push_surface is\npassed surface_local_dirty_rect), so the optimisation is preserved; inside a\nfilter surface it is surface_rects.clipped_local, the inflated region that\nsurface needs. This is also the rect prepare_quad_impl already uses to decide\nwhat to draw, so the two now agree.\n\nprepare_image_quads' tiled path had the same bug, from the same\ncompute_conservative_visible_rect(current_dirty_region()) call. It is worse\nthere: that rect culls the repetitions and, within each repetition, the\nindividual texture cache tiles, so even a plain non-repeating tiled image loses\nthe tiles that fall in the blur's margin, and those tiles are never requested\nfrom the resource cache at all. Both callers now share\ncompute_surface_visible_rect, and compute_conservative_visible_rect goes away\nwith its last caller.\n\nThe reftests put a repeating gradient, a repeating tiled image and a plain tiled\nimage inside a horizontally blurred surface that straddles the x=1024 picture\ncache tile boundary, and invalidate only the tiles on one side of it so that the\ndirty region ends mid-surface. Each reference needs a first frame that\ninvalidates every tile: the harness renders the reference into the same wrench\ninstance right after the test, so a reference display list identical to the\ntest's last frame invalidates nothing and merely re-composites the test's own\ntiles, reproducing whatever the test got wrong.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319789\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322328\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-repeat-gradient-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-repeat-gradient.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-repeat-tiled-image-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-repeat-tiled-image.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-tiled-image-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-tiled-image.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/reftest.list"], "git_node": "158ec65489699d9aeb4f65abba13bf45f36e1c5b", "git_parents": ["b221ec65c96a0a333db533571ad749a68796faef"], "node": "fec61f9d2db8de4f3effe91dc4e70fee4600ba9d", "parents": ["302fbfe9a9dfcb5f2f77c58f0ffb0cb9880b233f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788199178, "git_changesets": ["158ec65489699d9aeb4f65abba13bf45f36e1c5b"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "472": {"changesets": [{"author": "Maurice Dauer \u003cmdauer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057121 - Handle uniforms that are optimized out by TranslatorHLSL.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nAdapted backport of upstream ANGLE commit 82a623fafe0bcfdb4ae2f8dd3e13205584a64d42.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322357\n", "files": ["gfx/angle/checkout/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/ProgramD3D.cpp"], "git_node": "c515bec426fa04d1c6837606de081fe112f99a98", "git_parents": ["158ec65489699d9aeb4f65abba13bf45f36e1c5b"], "node": "b3af583beb5f6aae6f0fafa6cee4412e09de98b9", "parents": ["fec61f9d2db8de4f3effe91dc4e70fee4600ba9d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788199201, "git_changesets": ["c515bec426fa04d1c6837606de081fe112f99a98"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "473": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054021 - Also run selectedness algorithm when removing options of a combobox if there's no selected option.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321553\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322360\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/selected-index.html"], "git_node": "286a13537bf7de85ad4fa86ed82f95fa9a23c181", "git_parents": ["c515bec426fa04d1c6837606de081fe112f99a98"], "node": "933bd2c35b74e2e8b0e244e007944b5b3e41322e", "parents": ["b3af583beb5f6aae6f0fafa6cee4412e09de98b9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788199225, "git_changesets": ["286a13537bf7de85ad4fa86ed82f95fa9a23c181"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "474": {"changesets": [{"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062896 - Gate panel-list's click-on-mouseup on an explicit attribute instead of the anchor's role.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nBehavior-neutral: the new attribute is set on the two panel-lists whose anchors carry role=\"combobox\" today, the search mode switcher's and moz-select's.\n\n(cherry picked from commit b76836d1ddffbd90b4499c934dab09bab5f9f315)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322374\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_panel_item_mouseup_click.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-select/moz-select.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.mjs"], "git_node": "762d08ea43eb4f6c89ebb5749c445a02e39c49ad", "git_parents": ["286a13537bf7de85ad4fa86ed82f95fa9a23c181"], "node": "f8e08f148a0c10a0b130bfe995695c72248e1996", "parents": ["933bd2c35b74e2e8b0e244e007944b5b3e41322e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062896 - Stop exposing the search mode switcher as a combobox wrapping a button.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nRemoving the role outright, as suggested in bug 2009628 comment 18, leaves the host exposing an unnamed container: every moz-button host produces one, which bug 2064122 tracks.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 05d609cbcb212fc730d521592751fcd1418b707f)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322375\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_a11y.js"], "git_node": "f3d37ca30c1e23bcd5311567d23d58194564621c", "git_parents": ["762d08ea43eb4f6c89ebb5749c445a02e39c49ad"], "node": "a822c9953328bb64b34af8afaedc3c214a37085d", "parents": ["f8e08f148a0c10a0b130bfe995695c72248e1996"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065724 - Stop naming the search mode switcher \"More options\".  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\n`moz-button` maps `aria-label` onto its shadow button, so the hardcoded value became the control's accessible name while the engine-specific string only ever reaches `title`. The name is now computed from the button's content, i.e. the slotted `searchmode-switcher-dropmarker` image's own label, \"Pick a Search Engine\"; `title` supplies the description.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 302c03fbe9863bd12eddf253778dbbfd8cf0bed1)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322376\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_a11y.js"], "git_node": "cebd24352baf8705300969632592ac36d7185b54", "git_parents": ["f3d37ca30c1e23bcd5311567d23d58194564621c"], "node": "a75e90c399949bf8b3313f3365249cc86a4403ad", "parents": ["a822c9953328bb64b34af8afaedc3c214a37085d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788199250, "git_changesets": ["762d08ea43eb4f6c89ebb5749c445a02e39c49ad", "f3d37ca30c1e23bcd5311567d23d58194564621c", "cebd24352baf8705300969632592ac36d7185b54"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "475": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065138 - Honor checkDefaultBrowser pref for campaign set default actions  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320232\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322380\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/actors/AboutWelcomeParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_campaign_actions.js"], "git_node": "36da1d41ee87ef8242369ff5d0942d2f8a07d809", "git_parents": ["cebd24352baf8705300969632592ac36d7185b54"], "node": "35c8b43c979a2ac65fccc29bea5d61105fbcd065", "parents": ["a75e90c399949bf8b3313f3365249cc86a4403ad"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788199275, "git_changesets": ["36da1d41ee87ef8242369ff5d0942d2f8a07d809"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "476": {"changesets": [{"author": "Micah Killoran \u003cmtigley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045289 - Reformat moz-label accesskeys when the label text changes while not observing.  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319248\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322366\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_label.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-label/moz-label.mjs"], "git_node": "4c44db709cbf32765dbbbc25a304864b35e28221", "git_parents": ["36da1d41ee87ef8242369ff5d0942d2f8a07d809"], "node": "36d611e53094f3f4961edaff43ef45898afff04f", "parents": ["35c8b43c979a2ac65fccc29bea5d61105fbcd065"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788199637, "git_changesets": ["4c44db709cbf32765dbbbc25a304864b35e28221"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "477": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan Grulich \u003cjgrulich@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054622 - WebRTC backport: PipeWire mmap improvements  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nPipeWire: encapsulate mmap in ScopedBuf and fix mapoffset handling\nMove mmap into ScopedBuf::initialize so callers no longer manage mmap\nflags and cleanup directly. Use MAP_PRIVATE for read-only MemFd\nconsumers and MAP_SHARED for DmaBuf and read-write consumers. Fix\nscreen capture's double mapoffset application by passing the offset\nto mmap directly. Add AccessMode and BufferType enums for clarity\nand delete copy/move to prevent double-munmap.\n\nPipeWire: validate fd backing size before mmap\nValidate that the fd actually backs the requested mapping range\nby calling fstat and checking mapoffset + maxsize \u003c= st_size\nbefore mmap, matching what PipeWire does in its own memory pool\n(src/pipewire/mem.c). Skip the check for DmaBuf fds where fstat\ndoes not reliably report the buffer size.\n\nThis is a simple backport of WebRTC upstream changes.\n\nUpstream commits:\nc84dbe590a5519bc1404a268dd8816088ffe8980\n5c10f93376c1e9f0ff339bd1facf5b6d7d978f25\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321791\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322291\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/linux/wayland/shared_screencast_stream.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/linux/wayland/test/test_egl_dmabuf.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/linux/wayland/test/test_screencast_stream_provider.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/portal/pipewire_utils.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/portal/pipewire_utils.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_capture/linux/video_capture_pipewire.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/5c10f93376.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/c84dbe590a.no-op-cherry-pick-msg"], "git_node": "4e5885a63535616b74e958f4e7e98b27f42b2753", "git_parents": ["4c44db709cbf32765dbbbc25a304864b35e28221"], "node": "7a721f04110bf5720da6b84efba29a710bccd030", "parents": ["36d611e53094f3f4961edaff43ef45898afff04f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788220558, "git_changesets": ["4e5885a63535616b74e958f4e7e98b27f42b2753"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "478": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065646 - Unwrap about:reader URLs with ReaderMode.getOriginalUrl in WebsiteFilter.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321920\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322359\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/helpers/WebsiteFilter.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_websitefilter.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_websitefilter.js"], "git_node": "84092ad81d9137d7a34516decaf7a6bd908890f2", "git_parents": ["4e5885a63535616b74e958f4e7e98b27f42b2753"], "node": "0b2a86f0800c42af8a3d856e233c587b84518b21", "parents": ["7a721f04110bf5720da6b84efba29a710bccd030"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788220580, "git_changesets": ["84092ad81d9137d7a34516decaf7a6bd908890f2"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "479": {"changesets": [{"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061295: Hold a reference to nsDataObj in callbacks  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nAs the comment in `WaitForCompletion` explains, it does a SpinEventLoopUntil\nas part of CStream callbacks, and the CStream can be unregistered during that,\nwhich is fine, but we need to hold a strong reference first since we use\nthe object afterward.  The reference in `WaitForCompletion` is technically\nredundant but makes future uses safer and admits a comment that future clients\nmay actually heed.\n\nIt also adds an unrelated missing null check.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321699\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322409\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsDataObj.cpp"], "git_node": "e502b50d0f50fa877caef40ebd9eb8f6c3d2b1b3", "git_parents": ["84092ad81d9137d7a34516decaf7a6bd908890f2"], "node": "6635cc30e710f9913ee7acc420209e2a8211aee2", "parents": ["0b2a86f0800c42af8a3d856e233c587b84518b21"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788220601, "git_changesets": ["e502b50d0f50fa877caef40ebd9eb8f6c3d2b1b3"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "480": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicholas Rishel \u003cnrishel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061499 - Add UploadInitMemTracker to manage zeroing memory for partial texture uploads and marking uninitialized memory as initialized.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321124\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321996\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLTextureUpload.cpp", "dom/canvas/gtest/TestWebGLTextureUploadInit.cpp", "dom/canvas/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "04f4d67c02cbaaa5c4d898fba336cb29d2dc07c2", "git_parents": ["e502b50d0f50fa877caef40ebd9eb8f6c3d2b1b3"], "node": "35ef6609e53b75719abd019b4ba893823af85fb9", "parents": ["6635cc30e710f9913ee7acc420209e2a8211aee2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788220622, "git_changesets": ["04f4d67c02cbaaa5c4d898fba336cb29d2dc07c2"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "481": {"changesets": [{"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056051: Don't cancel the ImageDecoder read request from cycle-collection unlink  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318221\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322314\n", "files": ["dom/base/NodeIterator.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageDecoder.h"], "git_node": "a498955c972e3f6821040a6cef48268e5b2c1ba0", "git_parents": ["04f4d67c02cbaaa5c4d898fba336cb29d2dc07c2"], "node": "dba03aead4c765e9faab4c5768a13a15aeed1f8d", "parents": ["35ef6609e53b75719abd019b4ba893823af85fb9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788220646, "git_changesets": ["a498955c972e3f6821040a6cef48268e5b2c1ba0"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "482": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan Hunt \u003crhunt@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059577 - Track inlinedCallerOffsetsIndex per inline frame.  a=dmeehan\n\nRootCompiler stored inlinedCallerOffsetsIndex_ as a single shared field, but it\nis really a per-inlined-function value. finishInlineCall popped\ninlinedCallerOffsets_ without restoring the index, so TrapSiteDesc/CallSiteDesc\ncreated in the caller after an inlined call carried the finished callee's index\nand reported phantom inlined frames.\n\nMove the index onto FunctionCompiler, which is already constructed and destroyed\nper inline frame, and have startInlineCall hand it back for the callee compiler.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320554\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322406\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/inlining-stack-trace.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmIonCompile.cpp"], "git_node": "15a726468dfdb223039d7325da0dd30c809db839", "git_parents": ["a498955c972e3f6821040a6cef48268e5b2c1ba0"], "node": "f667132e4c6606b36d8f0d47c5bc19f611357f06", "parents": ["dba03aead4c765e9faab4c5768a13a15aeed1f8d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788220998, "git_changesets": ["15a726468dfdb223039d7325da0dd30c809db839"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "483": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 1ace7e56a446a26f61ef013ac6967e8186f47704 with FIREFOX_140_15_0esr_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "7709e79925134e7c0ddcc5780846609a1dddfbf2", "git_parents": ["ba9168741ea89dcb6c6d6ee3ce13cba9f65404