tps://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322843\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323353\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/DrawTargetCairo.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetCairo.h"], "git_node": "82eb3a837b44c391dd56c08736d88f80b78331bb", "git_parents": ["17a4b96bd2bd14e48df1d055c81b732f7cc9ad42"], "node": "53806eb850a08708452f9e1bf12e98f4ad22a682", "parents": ["b1a6139dd2aebd60aa856a2d388548934cadc13c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788543562, "git_changesets": ["82eb3a837b44c391dd56c08736d88f80b78331bb"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "497": {"changesets": [{"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067531: Add two Windows App SDK DLLs to the Firefox packager r=sylvestre a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322798\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323308\n", "files": ["browser/installer/package-manifest.in", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-WindowsAppSDK.sh", "toolkit/content/license.html", "widget/windows/moz.build"], "git_node": "a6dd277f381807482db2065e1c423f203f14045d", "git_parents": ["82eb3a837b44c391dd56c08736d88f80b78331bb"], "node": "7bd227a39e14861f183fe5a6dbf5aac7dffd1fae", "parents": ["53806eb850a08708452f9e1bf12e98f4ad22a682"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788543588, "git_changesets": ["a6dd277f381807482db2065e1c423f203f14045d"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "498": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049342: Use thread safe manager for prefix sets.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318398\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323291\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/url-classifier/VariableLengthPrefixSet.cpp", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/VariableLengthPrefixSet.h", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/tests/gtest/TestUrlClassifierPrefixSetReporter.cpp", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "8ae5879e1848f1e1db0e41e819f8e68fce9c611c", "git_parents": ["a6dd277f381807482db2065e1c423f203f14045d"], "node": "11607754e59e12ba10c2e5987f25f592c8834ab5", "parents": ["7bd227a39e14861f183fe5a6dbf5aac7dffd1fae"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788543739, "git_changesets": ["8ae5879e1848f1e1db0e41e819f8e68fce9c611c"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "499": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kui-Feng Lee \u003cthinker.li@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058664 - Give WaylandMonitor one owner instead of one per callback.  a=dmeehan\n\nWaylandMonitor gives a raw pointer to four Wayland listeners, and three of them\nkeep it alive: each takes a reference that its own callback releases when it\nruns. Finish() destroys the wp_image_description_v1 one of those listeners is\nattached to, which cancels its callback. A cancelled callback never runs, so it\nnever releases its reference, and the monitor is never freed.\n\nNo misbehaviour is needed to hit this. When a display profile changes, the\ncompositor tells us the output's colour setup changed\n(image_description_changed). Firefox answers by starting a fresh screen\nenumeration, which finishes the previous one. Finishing destroys the image\ndescription that monitor is still waiting on, so the reply never arrives and\nthe reference taken to wait for it is never released. Sending the colour change\nbefore the reply reproduces it: the monitor's destructor never runs.\n\nTwo objects are also never destroyed at all: the one\nwp_image_description_v1_get_information() returns, which ImageDescriptionReady()\ndrops, and the wl_callback from wl_display_sync(), which Finish() drops. Each\nleaks once per monitor per screen enumeration. Each also leaves a listener\npointing at the monitor after it is gone, so a malicious or broken compositor\nthat sends an event after done writes through a stale pointer.\n\nGive the monitor a single owner. mWaylandMonitors holds it, and every listener\nthat does work on it takes a scoped reference for as long as it runs, so no\ncallback can outlive what it is using. Finish() destroys every object a listener is\nattached to, so nothing can reach a monitor the getter is about to release.\n\nThat makes the reference Finish() took redundant. It covered the same window -\na callback on the stack when ScreenGetterGtk::Finish() clears mWaylandMonitors\n- by holding the monitor until a compositor round-trip completed. The\nwl_display.sync goes with it, and so does the wl_callback it was leaking.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320580\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323700\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/ScreenHelperGTK.cpp"], "git_node": "b72c058132c1aa53e4ce42228b744fc784663caf", "git_parents": ["8ae5879e1848f1e1db0e41e819f8e68fce9c611c"], "node": "f98fb3973a60efde953892e8b39870f69953980e", "parents": ["11607754e59e12ba10c2e5987f25f592c8834ab5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788544933, "git_changesets": ["b72c058132c1aa53e4ce42228b744fc784663caf"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "500": {"changesets": [{"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067971.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322591\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323204\n", "files": ["image/decoders/nsJPEGDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "2df030f430a8aa5458e208395774f9afc50b7c2d", "git_parents": ["b72c058132c1aa53e4ce42228b744fc784663caf"], "node": "7db8af1f7861c0c3e3e0c8efcc21d50bd394948d", "parents": ["f98fb3973a60efde953892e8b39870f69953980e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788550078, "git_changesets": ["2df030f430a8aa5458e208395774f9afc50b7c2d"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "501": {"changesets": [{"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068354 - Check whether we're reflowing when observing changes  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323194\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323332\n", "files": ["layout/svg/SVGObserverUtils.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGTextFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "99741994a22ab0004f47d4a0e2ed0face26752c3", "git_parents": ["2df030f430a8aa5458e208395774f9afc50b7c2d"], "node": "ced3e77e4d7be5881c7ca804aa1f41a66d59e2e1", "parents": ["7db8af1f7861c0c3e3e0c8efcc21d50bd394948d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788550099, "git_changesets": ["99741994a22ab0004f47d4a0e2ed0face26752c3"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "502": {"changesets": [{"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068438  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323156\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323435\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ImageContainer.cpp", "gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.cpp", "gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.h"], "git_node": "261eda41ad98590ad4621bfa7fa15adced5240f7", "git_parents": ["99741994a22ab0004f47d4a0e2ed0face26752c3"], "node": "54c3abf3c7a1ab0761a85b3cc78abf8c83d20fba", "parents": ["ced3e77e4d7be5881c7ca804aa1f41a66d59e2e1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788550120, "git_changesets": ["261eda41ad98590ad4621bfa7fa15adced5240f7"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "503": {"changesets": [{"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061777 - Reject parent-only Client ops received from content processes.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321169\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323521\n", "files": ["dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleOpParent.cpp"], "git_node": "742d76ae45a8bf523bcd1c81f689c87b52a487c1", "git_parents": ["261eda41ad98590ad4621bfa7fa15adced5240f7"], "node": "717f481ec3f8ea3d5cdd7ecf719867fc58e67206", "parents": ["54c3abf3c7a1ab0761a85b3cc78abf8c83d20fba"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788550162, "git_changesets": ["742d76ae45a8bf523bcd1c81f689c87b52a487c1"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "504": {"changesets": [{"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068445 - Detach canvas observer when we reassign the filter  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322926\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323583\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp"], "git_node": "7c22c83ffb8673d91c35b08e2f66751d394825bf", "git_parents": ["742d76ae45a8bf523bcd1c81f689c87b52a487c1"], "node": "70b5a6007e8f51e79a42b43c8ebd4d038b689c9a", "parents": ["717f481ec3f8ea3d5cdd7ecf719867fc58e67206"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788550420, "git_changesets": ["7c22c83ffb8673d91c35b08e2f66751d394825bf"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "505": {"changesets": [{"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068433 - Assert buffer is same-compartment in fromBufferSameCompartment  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323377\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323641\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/TypedArrayObject.cpp"], "git_node": "ee3ac245db5a18895e0d72a9929b019a8a622239", "git_parents": ["7c22c83ffb8673d91c35b08e2f66751d394825bf"], "node": "5060191c211e4e7a478f03845598a312dacfefa6", "parents": ["70b5a6007e8f51e79a42b43c8ebd4d038b689c9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068433 - Wrap buffer  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323378\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323642\n", "files": ["dom/streams/ReadableByteStreamController.cpp"], "git_node": "a87242f82f2c915acc7438893540a20ce1db6177", "git_parents": ["ee3ac245db5a18895e0d72a9929b019a8a622239"], "node": "c7b5b775e5f5e116effde2bffbe1e82b4a0b3c63", "parents": ["5060191c211e4e7a478f03845598a312dacfefa6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788616292, "git_changesets": ["ee3ac245db5a18895e0d72a9929b019a8a622239", "a87242f82f2c915acc7438893540a20ce1db6177"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "506": {"changesets": [{"author": "DonalMe \u003c76789979+DonalMe@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068433 - Fix code formatting a=bustage DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/TypedArrayObject.cpp"], "git_node": "fb47e0741dec94f0cb5b025da31b0a5999917611", "git_parents": ["a87242f82f2c915acc7438893540a20ce1db6177"], "node": "81d50f37a5ada5bf65f5d5925867c334667f34c8", "parents": ["c7b5b775e5f5e116effde2bffbe1e82b4a0b3c63"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788616499, "git_changesets": ["fb47e0741dec94f0cb5b025da31b0a5999917611"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "507": {"changesets": [{"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011632: Adjust directv WebCompat intervention to more narrowly target the affected site.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nThe point of our intervention here was to address a UA-sniffing-based block on\nthe stream.directv.com website. Our intervention has been targeting\nall subdomains of directv.com, which turns out to have been unnecessary and\ncounterproductive, becuase the UA override breaks the directv login flow in\nsome way.\n\nThis patch narrows the intervention to *only* target stream.directv.com. With\nthat, I've confirmed that login works again and I can still access the\nstreaming page.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320973\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323753\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1728450-directv.com.json"], "git_node": "a92746c7e3b4479fcdcf5bdff102e6631a5026a0", "git_parents": ["fb47e0741dec94f0cb5b025da31b0a5999917611"], "node": "28d11ff04fe519386defa97ca95293c5481da93e", "parents": ["81d50f37a5ada5bf65f5d5925867c334667f34c8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788617057, "git_changesets": ["a92746c7e3b4479fcdcf5bdff102e6631a5026a0"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "508": {"changesets": [{"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068361 - modernize ChromeTooltipListener a bit,  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323365\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323525\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShellTreeOwner.cpp"], "git_node": "61d3a10ec9d551ad47132e21aaeda07fe6b467aa", "git_parents": ["a92746c7e3b4479fcdcf5bdff102e6631a5026a0"], "node": "e23006eeb2a87d04d6eef40fc488e55b0ad513bc", "parents": ["28d11ff04fe519386defa97ca95293c5481da93e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788617081, "git_changesets": ["61d3a10ec9d551ad47132e21aaeda07fe6b467aa"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "509": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068440 - Validate fieldset listed elements.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nMake sure we have a fieldset. We can't check _which_ fieldset because\nfieldset.elements work across multiple fieldsets.\n\nTrack elements inside legends and check the disabled-ness more\nexplicitly instead.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322883\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323531\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLFieldSetElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/form-associated/fieldset-elements-after-upgrade.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/form-associated/fieldset-elements-during-construction.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/form-associated/form-disabled-legend.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-fieldset-element/disabled-nested-legend.html"], "git_node": "4db9a61087452a2443bb4809b38cc1eb1bc974ed", "git_parents": ["61d3a10ec9d551ad47132e21aaeda07fe6b467aa"], "node": "60674b7b98cbe3bd0c2b9b328264caae8dbb6d3f", "parents": ["e23006eeb2a87d04d6eef40fc488e55b0ad513bc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788617107, "git_changesets": ["4db9a61087452a2443bb4809b38cc1eb1bc974ed"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "510": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr153 repo-update HSTS HPKP -  a=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323812\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": "c6e3046c0a9fd51535004d5ad726f8a9320cf1f9", "git_parents": ["4db9a61087452a2443bb4809b38cc1eb1bc974ed"], "node": "7b7ff9dd131ddee61f5f969f56401861bc2fbd2c", "parents": ["60674b7b98cbe3bd0c2b9b328264caae8dbb6d3f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788617400, "git_changesets": ["c6e3046c0a9fd51535004d5ad726f8a9320cf1f9"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "511": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066814 - Restrict the properties that highlight pseudos get at cascade time.  a=dmeehan\n\nMatches Chrome and the spec in terms of em / lh units etc, and prevents\nborder-radius to set the border-background flag without extra tracking.\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/357\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323848\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/gecko/pseudo_element.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/pseudo_element_definition.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/cascade.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/rule_cache.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/highlight-cascade/highlight-cascade-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/forced-colors-mode/forced-colors-mode-14.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/selection-background-color-non-applicable-properties-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/selection-background-color-non-applicable-properties.html"], "git_node": "2fd9b2919f32138263d5b26d277083be9cb16366", "git_parents": ["c6e3046c0a9fd51535004d5ad726f8a9320cf1f9"], "node": "45e6eba279626dae569c8d893d9c35d97ce417a4", "parents": ["7b7ff9dd131ddee61f5f969f56401861bc2fbd2c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788704074, "git_changesets": ["2fd9b2919f32138263d5b26d277083be9cb16366"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "512": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr153 repo-update remote-settings tld-suffixes ct-logs -  a=pascalc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323961\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/ai-window-prompts.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/newtab-wallpapers-v2.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-config-v2.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/translations-models.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": "a7eb387766f22ad118f66b6238c8e4a318074dfc", "git_parents": ["2fd9b2919f32138263d5b26d277083be9cb16366"], "node": "b9cbedc575c70b2d173c10fa03df595f622bb9b5", "parents": ["45e6eba279626dae569c8d893d9c35d97ce417a4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788761793, "git_changesets": ["a7eb387766f22ad118f66b6238c8e4a318074dfc"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "513": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mathieu Leplatre \u003cmathieu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065636 - Simplify error handling branches in _importChanges  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322645\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323516\n", "files": ["services/settings/RemoteSettingsClient.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f65969e523a236386ed646206ecd2081cad52b06", "git_parents": ["a7eb387766f22ad118f66b6238c8e4a318074dfc"], "node": "26a8a8260cefb5fd5a394ebf3507866ae340a035", "parents": ["b9cbedc575c70b2d173c10fa03df595f622bb9b5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788810759, "git_changesets": ["f65969e523a236386ed646206ecd2081cad52b06"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "514": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mathieu Leplatre \u003cmathieu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068952 - Handle verification failures consistently in _importChanges  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323231\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323519\n", "files": ["services/settings/RemoteSettingsClient.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c9abca33c98c3a2ae7a34bad6d6e7138dd7e1981", "git_parents": ["f65969e523a236386ed646206ecd2081cad52b06"], "node": "a434398facf58adf35a9ea9e33a099cf5dfe0715", "parents": ["26a8a8260cefb5fd5a394ebf3507866ae340a035"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788810913, "git_changesets": ["c9abca33c98c3a2ae7a34bad6d6e7138dd7e1981"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "515": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067436: Don't allow the viewport cache for non-doc accessibles.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323141\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323951\n", "files": ["accessible/ipc/RemoteAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "a45de47b3dfb36aa379acce4454913f18de657ad", "git_parents": ["c9abca33c98c3a2ae7a34bad6d6e7138dd7e1981"], "node": "8e6f014d314e3476a4faf64ad91f6c7fa97b16de", "parents": ["a434398facf58adf35a9ea9e33a099cf5dfe0715"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788810936, "git_changesets": ["a45de47b3dfb36aa379acce4454913f18de657ad"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "516": {"changesets": [{"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068442 - Make `EditorBase::InsertTextIntoTextNodeWithTransaction` not use `CompositionTransaction` if it's not caused by a composition change  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\n`insertText` command etc may be used during a composition and we need\nto handle them for the backward compatibility and compatibility with\nthe other browsers.\n\nHowever, we should not treat such coming commands as a part of\ncomposition. Therefore, we should make the related methods take\n`InputTextFor` and consider to make an `InsertTextTransaction` for\na text insertion not caused by a composition change.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323152\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323954\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/EditorBase.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorBase.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditSubActionHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.h", "editor/libeditor/TextEditSubActionHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/WhiteSpaceVisibilityKeeper.cpp", "editor/libeditor/WhiteSpaceVisibilityKeeper.h"], "git_node": "e91c620c2ed8b5b9b29441c8346d7cb99a630034", "git_parents": ["a45de47b3dfb36aa379acce4454913f18de657ad"], "node": "ab23e8c937474b2388a1c33e207a3a5b3b92606e", "parents": ["8e6f014d314e3476a4faf64ad91f6c7fa97b16de"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788810960, "git_changesets": ["e91c620c2ed8b5b9b29441c8346d7cb99a630034"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "517": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043770 - Initialize the test SEI payload so the HVCC-\u003eAnnexB round-trip length is deterministic.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nGetHvccExtraDataWithPrefixSEI appended the SEI payload with\nnsTArray::AppendElements(count), which default-initializes and so leaves the\nPOD bytes uninitialized. With the mozjemalloc defaults (no junk/zero fill on\nalloc), the payload reads as 0x00 whenever it lands on a fresh OS-zeroed chunk.\nOn the MOZ_WMF SEI-filtering path that makes EncodeH265NALUnit insert\nemulation-prevention bytes and inflate the converted length past the expected\nvalue, while a recycled (free-poisoned) chunk does not. The outcome depends only\non heap layout, so the H265.HVCCToAnnexB* gtests failed intermittently and\nturned permanent once an unrelated allocation change shifted the layout.\n\nFill the payload with a fixed non-zero pattern so no emulation-prevention bytes\nare produced and the round-trip size is deterministic.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308210\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323983\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/agnostic/bytestreams/gtest/TestByteStreams.cpp"], "git_node": "faf667e2ed6ddf6a93749e6ccb3d2c2a3a63bbd3", "git_parents": ["e91c620c2ed8b5b9b29441c8346d7cb99a630034"], "node": "451aa3c582c510e42d7546a4e05fb48ba9ff4943", "parents": ["ab23e8c937474b2388a1c33e207a3a5b3b92606e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788811015, "git_changesets": ["faf667e2ed6ddf6a93749e6ccb3d2c2a3a63bbd3"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "518": {"changesets": [{"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068378 - Dispatch pass-through OnDataAvailable to the main thread in nsHTTPCompressConv  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nRead the data and hand it to do_OnDataAvailable() when a bounce is\nneeded; keep the direct pass-through otherwise.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322964\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323958\n", "files": ["netwerk/streamconv/converters/nsHTTPCompressConv.cpp"], "git_node": "62745e8e45f39145368e0510e9b7a7b253873dd6", "git_parents": ["faf667e2ed6ddf6a93749e6ccb3d2c2a3a63bbd3"], "node": "40ddbf365547e3e5099a9eb73347d840be65e083", "parents": ["451aa3c582c510e42d7546a4e05fb48ba9ff4943"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788811039, "git_changesets": ["62745e8e45f39145368e0510e9b7a7b253873dd6"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "519": {"changesets": [{"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2001265 - Enforce Local Network Access checks on notification icon loads  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nNotification icon loads have no requesting node, so their LoadInfo has no\nbrowsing context and the parent IP address space resolved to Unknown, which\nmakes IsLocalOrPrivateNetworkAccess() false for any target. Read the address\nspace from the policy container instead, which Document::InitPolicyContainer\nalready propagates for exactly this reason, and share that resolution with\nthe two copies of it in nsHttpChannel.\n\nThese loads have no tab to anchor a permission prompt on, and can outlive the\npage that created the notification, so treat them like shared and service\nworker requests: never prompt, and only allow when the origin already has a\npersistent LNA permission.\n\nAlso add a regression test for the document CSP being applied to these loads.\nThat already works, since bug 1997282 moved icon decoding into the content\nprocess and the load carries the creating global's ClientInfo, but it is the\nother half of this bug and was untested.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319466\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323998\n", "files": ["dom/notification/test/mochitest/file_notification_icon_csp.html", "dom/notification/test/mochitest/file_notification_icon_csp_self.html", "dom/notification/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/notification/test/mochitest/test_notification_icon_csp.html", "netwerk/base/LNAPermissionRequest.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/browser/browser.toml", "netwerk/test/browser/browser_test_local_network_access_notification.js", "netwerk/test/browser/page_notification_icon.html"], "git_node": "6d3acc35092e4a8413ba5fed34de96d8d3d24b29", "git_parents": ["62745e8e45f39145368e0510e9b7a7b253873dd6"], "node": "0dd9c2824fb78751de23c44be326c68fe91826df", "parents": ["40ddbf365547e3e5099a9eb73347d840be65e083"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788811064, "git_changesets": ["6d3acc35092e4a8413ba5fed34de96d8d3d24b29"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "520": {"changesets": [{"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061327 - Uncache subtree of hidden accessible when it is coalesced.  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319920\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324077\n", "files": ["accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "1e10d63baf4de55eb41c62ed59d15d7032c92ccf", "git_parents": ["6d3acc35092e4a8413ba5fed34de96d8d3d24b29"], "node": "07e755843216b97670bb2b1c66a7c5b21ca708fc", "parents": ["0dd9c2824fb78751de23c44be326c68fe91826df"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788811545, "git_changesets": ["1e10d63baf4de55eb41c62ed59d15d7032c92ccf"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "521": {"changesets": [{"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064287 - Harden drag handling;  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321984\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324122\n", "files": ["dom/base/PointerLockManager.cpp", "dom/base/PointerLockManager.h", "dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.h", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h", "widget/nsBaseDragService.cpp", "widget/nsIDragService.idl"], "git_node": "861fdeb0d32fe1bd101fea886687e680f612d735", "git_parents": ["1e10d63baf4de55eb41c62ed59d15d7032c92ccf"], "node": "3b49a44994fb7ff6902f7df5a3bd5f689a4fb4e9", "parents": ["07e755843216b97670bb2b1c66a7c5b21ca708fc"], "tags": ["FIREFOX_153_3_0esr_BUILD1", "FIREFOX_153_3_0esr_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1788879760, "git_changesets": ["861fdeb0d32fe1bd101fea886687e680f612d735"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}}
}";